Eggplant Parmesan Meatballs
  --Jamie Vespa

1 1/2 lbs eggplant, cut into 1×1-inch cubes (about 2 medium globe eggplants)
6 tbsp evoo, divided
3/4 tsp kosher salt
1 c + 2 tbsp seasoned breadcrumbs (sub plain breadcrumbs mixed with 1 tsp Italian seasoning)
1/3 c grated Parmesan cheese (+ more for garnish)
1/4 c chopped fresh parsley
1 whole egg + 1 egg yolk, whisked
3 garlic cloves, thinly sliced or minced
1/2 tsp black pepper
1/2 tsp onion powder
24-oz jar marinara sauce
1/2 c whole-milk ricotta cheese
Crusty bread for serving

Preheat oven to 375F. Place eggplant in a 13×9" baking dish; toss with 3 tbsp olive oil and salt. Bake for 30 min, tossing once once halfway through. Let chill for 15-20 min, until cool enough to handle. (Keep the oven at 375F.) Place eggplant in a food processor and pulse ~10-12 times, or until the eggplant is finely chopped/broken down. Add breadcrumbs, Parmesan, parsley, eggs, garlic, black pepper, and onion powder. Continue pulsing until the mixture is well-combined. Form into 20 mini meatballs (~2 tbsp each). Heat 2 tbsp oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Once hot, add half the meatballs and cook for 6-7 min, turning to cook all sides, until browned. Repeat with second batch of eggplant meatballs, adding another 1 tbsp oil as needed to the pan. Spread marinara sauce in the same 13×9" baking pan you roasted the eggplant in. Arrange eggplant meatballs in the pan, along with dollops of ricotta cheese throughout. Bake at 375F for 15-18 min, until the marinara is bubbly. Garnish with extra fresh chopped parsley and Parmesan cheese. Serve warm with crusty bread. 

Notes: Can roast the eggplant up to two days ahead and keep refrigerated in an airtight container. Mixture can be too moist
